---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import { ViewSwitcherNarrow, ViewSwitcherPlayground, ViewSwitcherUnavailable } from '../../components/ViewSwitcherDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs title="View Switcher" description="The bar of a table's open views, with an Add view menu.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">View Switcher</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    The bar of a table's open views, such as Table, List, Board, Chart and Timeline. An “Add view” menu explains each
    view. Your app decides which views exist, which are open and which can close. The switcher shows exactly what you
    pass and calls you back.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <ViewSwitcherPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Views of a table"
      code={`import { Grid } from "reicon-react/icons/Grid";
import { Kanban } from "reicon-react/icons/Kanban";
import { List } from "reicon-react/icons/List";
import { ViewSwitcher, viewSwitcherTabId } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/view-switcher";

const options = [
  { id: "table", label: "Table", icon: Grid, description: "Rows and columns. Edit, group and sum." },
  { id: "list", label: "List", icon: List, description: "One item per row for quick reading." },
  { id: "board", label: "Board", icon: Kanban, description: "Cards in lanes, one lane per stage.",
    unavailable: hasSingleSelect ? undefined : "Needs a single-select field." },
];

<ViewSwitcher
  views={open.map(id => ({ ...byId[id], closable: id !== "table" }))}
  value={layout}
  onValueChange={setLayout}
  options={options}
  onAdd={id => { if (!open.includes(id)) openView(id); setLayout(id); }}
  onClose={closeView}
  panelId="records"
  actions={<Button variant="ghost" size="icon-sm" aria-label="View settings">…</Button>}
/>
<div role="tabpanel" id="records" aria-labelledby={viewSwitcherTabId("records", layout)} tabIndex={0}>
  {layout === "board" ? <Board … /> : <Table … />}
</div>`}
    />
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>views</code>: <code>{'{ id, label, icon, closable? }[]'}</code>. The tabs, in order. <code>icon</code> is
        an icon component that takes <code>size</code>, such as one from <code>reicon-react</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>value</code> and <code>onValueChange</code>: the active view's <code>id</code>. Click and arrow keys call
        <code>onValueChange</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>options</code>: <code>{'{ id, label, icon, description, unavailable? }[]'}</code>. The views in the “Add
        view” menu. Leave it out to hide the menu.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>onAdd</code>: called with the chosen option. Options that are already in <code>views</code> show a check.
        Choosing one still calls <code>onAdd</code>; switch to that view there, as the example does.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>onClose</code>: called by a tab's close control or the Delete key. Only views marked
        <code>closable</code> can close, and only when you pass <code>onClose</code>. Remove the view from
        <code>views</code>, and pick a new <code>value</code> if the active view closed.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>actions</code>: controls at the end of the bar, such as a settings button.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>panelId</code>: the <code>id</code> of your panel. Every tab points to it with <code>aria-controls</code>.
        Label the panel with <code>viewSwitcherTabId(panelId, value)</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>label</code> and <code>addLabel</code>: the tab list's name, “Views” by default, and the menu button's
        text, “Add view” by default.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Views that cannot be added</h2>
    <p>
      Set <code>unavailable</code> to say why an option cannot be added. The menu shows the reason in place of the
      description, dims the icon and does not let anyone choose it.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ViewSwitcherUnavailable client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Narrow screens</h2>
    <p>
      When the tabs do not fit, they scroll sideways and fade at each edge that hides more tabs. The active tab scrolls
      into view. “Add view” and <code>actions</code> stay at the end. Under 480px the button shows only its plus icon,
      and the menu uses one column.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <ViewSwitcherNarrow client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The bar is a <code>tablist</code> named by <code>label</code>. It is one tab stop. Left and Right move between
      tabs and choose them at once; Home and End go to the first and last tab. On a closable tab, Delete (or Backspace)
      calls <code>onClose</code>. When the tab closes, focus moves to the view your app chose, or else to a neighbour.
      The close control is for the pointer only, so it is hidden from screen readers; the tab announces the Delete
      shortcut.
    </p>
    <p>
      The menu lists options in reading order, and the arrow keys move through them one by one. An unavailable option
      has <code>aria-disabled</code> and its reason as the description. An open option is described as “Already open”.
      Escape closes the menu and returns focus to “Add view”.
    </p>
    <p>The underline slides to the active tab over 180ms. It does not move when reduced motion is requested.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Tabs use <code>--sprout-muted</code> and, when active, <code>--sprout-text</code> with a<code>--sprout-text</code>{' '}
      underline over a <code>--sprout-line</code> rule. Hover uses <code>--sprout-hover</code>. The menu uses the
      Dropdown Menu surface; icon tiles use <code>--sprout-hover</code> and
      <code>--sprout-radius-control</code>. Motion uses <code>--sprout-motion-normal</code>,
      <code>--sprout-motion-fast</code> and <code>--sprout-motion-ease</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
